      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "There are a total of 7 marbles to choose from, and Johnny needs to select three. This is a combination problem, where order does not matter. The number of ways to choose three marbles out of seven is denoted as C(7,3) or \"$7 \\choose 3$\".\n\nTo calculate C(7,3), we use the formula given by:\n$$C(n,k) = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!},$$\nwhere n is the total number of options (marbles) and k is the number of items we want to select.\n\nSo,\n$$C(7,3) = \\frac{\\cancel{7}^{7}\\times\\cancel{6}^{6}\\times\\cancel{5}^{5}}{\\cancel{5}^{2}\\times\\cancel{4}^{3}\\times\\cancel{3}^{1}} = 35$$\n\nThus, Johnny can choose three marbles from his bag to play the game in $\\boxed{35}$ ways.",
